.TH SANCHALA-PERMISSIONS 1 "August 2026" "Sanchala OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sanchala-permissions \- Application permission manager (TCC-like) for Sanchala OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-permissions
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sanchala-permissions
provides macOS TCC-like permission management for applications,
controlling access to camera, microphone, location, files, and more.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIAPP\fR]
List permissions (all or for specific app)
.TP
.B grant \fIAPP\fR \fIPERMISSION\fR
Grant permission to application
.TP
.B revoke \fIAPP\fR \fIPERMISSION\fR
Revoke permission from application
.TP
.B reset \fIAPP\fR
Reset all permissions for application
.TP
.B audit \fR[\fIAPP\fR]
Show permission access log
.TP
.B requests
Show pending permission requests
.SH PERMISSIONS
camera, microphone, location, contacts, calendar, files, downloads,
desktop, documents, removable, network, notifications, accessibility,
automation, screen-recording, input-monitoring
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List all app permissions:
.B sanchala-permissions list
.TP
Grant camera to Zoom:
.B sanchala-permissions grant zoom camera
.TP
Show access audit:
.B sanchala-permissions audit firefox
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/permissions/
System policy
.TP
.I ~/.config/sanchala/permissions.db
User permission database
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sanchala-guardian (1),
.BR flatpak-permission (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sanchala OS Team <dev@sanchala.id>
